  "final_text": "**Proposed disposition:** ESCALATE, with confidence 0.72.\n\n**The three facts that drove it:**\n- The trader placed a one-sided SELL limit of 31,395, which is 12.9 times average top-5 depth, 3 ticks from the touch. It had no fills. About 2.8 seconds later the trader bought 1,053 by market order. The SELL was cancelled in full 158 ms after that.\n- The price moved 0.5 tick in the trader's favour, then reverted 2.5 ticks after the cancel.\n- No legitimate explanation holds. The trader's registered market making is on SYN.B, not SYN.A. The window has no market events, no risk events and no parent or pegged orders.\n\n**What would change my mind:** Evidence that the SELL was a genuine client or parent order, or that the price move and reversion were unrelated to it. A repeat of the cycle elsewhere in the session would instead support a STOR draft. I did not propose DRAFT_STOR because there is only one cycle, no prior alerts and no repetition.",
